cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ragbench, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "ragbench: evaluating RAG and agentic search on quality, latency and cost"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sean
    family-names: McRae
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/seanmcrae/ragbench"
url: "https://seanmcrae.github.io/ragbench/"
abstract: >-
  An evaluation harness that compares retrieval-augmented and agentic search pipelines on
  retrieval quality, answer quality, groundedness, latency and cost-to-serve, and recommends
  a configuration under a budget with paired bootstrap confidence intervals. Runs offline by
  default with a deterministic mock generator.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - information retrieval
  - evaluation
  - llm
  - agentic search
